cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "The System Point Cloud: genealogy and areality drawn from phonological correspondences alone"
abstract: >-
  A reconstruction-free, family-tree-free distance between documented language systems, defined as the mean number
  of phonological features that differ per aligned consonant slot across statistically detected coderivative sets.
  Embedding the distance matrix (MDS) and linking nearest neighbours makes a language family draw itself as a point
  cloud, in which genealogical branches and areal contact are legible without ever using branch labels to build the
  map. Companion to the pilot "Additive Structure of Phonological Correspondences".
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Toledo Martínez"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-1277-9697"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
